      "content": "but you keep saying \"not supported by evidence\" which feels like you've already decided the side that's complaining is wrong. if a system has openings that could be exploited, even if they haven't been \"proven\" yet, isn't it more honest to say the system is vulnerable? it feels like you're just defending the status quo instead of actually looking at why so many people are genuinely terrified that their vote isn't being counted right.",
